    <item>
      <title></title>
      <link>https://atcbosselut.github.io/authors/antoine/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>https://atcbosselut.github.io/authors/antoine/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;I am a PhD student at the University of Washington in the &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.cs.washington.edu/research/nlp&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34;&gt;Natural  Language Processing Group&lt;/a&gt; advised by Professor &lt;a href=&#34;https://homes.cs.washington.edu/~yejin&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34;&gt;Yejin Choi&lt;/a&gt;. My research centers on using deep learning to discover commonsense knowledge and simulate commonsense reasoning. I am also a researcher on the &lt;a href=&#34;https://mosaic.allenai.org&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34;&gt;Mosaic Project&lt;/a&gt; at the &lt;a href=&#34;https://allenai.org&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34;&gt;Allen Institute for Artificial Intelligence&lt;/a&gt;.
&lt;!--  and collaborate extensively with [Asli Celikyilmaz](https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/research/people/aslicel/) on the Deep Learning Team at MSR --&gt;
Check out my &lt;b&gt;&lt;a target=&#34;_blank&#34; href=&#34;files/cv.pdf&#34;&gt;CV&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; for more details.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;!-- I&#39;m always happy to discuss projects with prospective researchers and have advised multiple students throughout my time at the University of Washington. --&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
</description>
